==Problem==

Let <imath>\triangle ABC</imath> be a scalene triangle. Point <imath>P</imath> lies on <imath>\overline{BC}</imath> so that <imath>\overline{AP}</imath> bisects <imath>\angle BAC.</imath> The line through <imath>B</imath> perpendicular to <imath>\overline{AP}</imath> intersects the line through <imath>A</imath> parallel to <imath>\overline{BC}</imath> at point <imath>D.</imath> Suppose <imath>BP=2</imath> and <imath>PC=3.</imath> What is <imath>AD?</imath>

<imath>\textbf{(A) } 8 \qquad \textbf{(B) } 9 \qquad \textbf{(C) } 10 \qquad \textbf{(D) } 11 \qquad \textbf{(E) } 12</imath>

